    "done_when": "§7's selection paragraphs are the specification; read them whole before editing. The JT-60SA machine slug is jt-60sa everywhere the route reads it: maps/jt-60sa/machine_map.json, bundle.json, imas_ambix/gs/description_artifact.py MACHINE and the description reader already use it. imas_ambix/spine_bench/shots.py is the outlier: its JT60SA_FROZEN_SHOTSET shots declare machine=jt60sa and FROZEN_SHOTSETS keys that row jt60sa. Change both to jt-60sa, and make tests/spine_bench/test_shotset_labelling.py, tests/spine_bench/test_parity.py and tests/spine_bench/test_machine_artifact_arm.py follow. That way the machine the selector takes from the frozen set is one the pin table, the registry and the description reader accept. A test asserts that every FROZEN_SHOTSETS key equals the declared machine of each shot in its row, and that the JT-60SA key equals description_artifact.MACHINE. In imas_ambix/gs/artifact_resolution.py, PINNED_SEMANTIC_IDENTITY, PINNED_PHYSICAL_DIGEST and PINNED_REGISTRY_DIGEST retire into one table keyed by machine. Each machine's entry holds one row per pinned physical identity, carrying its semantic identity, physical digest, registry digest and authoring route. MAST's row holds today's three values, and its route is nova's publish_refined_artifact. JT-60SA has an OP1 row and an OP2 row, whose values are copied from the two artifacts imas_ambix/gs/description_artifact.py author_jt60sa_machine_artifacts authors at this node's base, and whose route is that producer. resolve_machine_description and author_pinned_description take the machine and the shot's physical digest. The digest may be omitted only for a one-row machine. Omitted for jt-60sa it is refused by name, and a digest the machine's entry does not hold is refused by name. In imas_ambix/gs/machine_identity.py, default_registry takes the machine and caches one registry per machine. mast returns nova's packaged registry, jt-60sa returns imas_ambix/gs/description_artifact.py build_jt60sa_registry_from_stores(), and any other machine is refused by name. identity_for_shot, and identity_for_representation's bare-digest form, gain a required machine keyword. identity_for_table and same_machine take the registry for the signature's machine, and identity_for_representation does the same when given a signature. imas_ambix/gs/machine_selection.py ArtifactMachineSelector gains a required machine. It resolves the registry, the acquisition read (read_acquisition_channels with that machine) and the geometry reader from it. It looks the shot's identity up first, then resolves the pin row and artifact by machine and that identity's physical digest. A machine missing from the pin table or the registry is refused by name at construction. select_machine, imas_ambix/gs/machine_geometry.py and imas_ambix/spine_bench/machine_artifact_arm.py each pass the machine once. imas_ambix/gs/artifact_geometry.py MachineArtifactGeometryReader.machine has no default, and _shot_evidence passes it on. machine_artifact_arm.py stops importing and re-exporting the PINNED_* names and reads its expected digests from the table row for its declared machine, the OP1 row for JT-60SA. The tests that read the PINNED_* names migrate to the table, and the bare-digest calls in tests/gs/test_machine_identity.py name mast. New tests in tests/gs/test_machine_selection.py show five things: a JT-60SA selector selects OP1 shot 101173 to the OP1 artifact, with a table whose signature machine is jt-60sa; resolve_machine_description('jt-60sa') with no digest raises naming the machine; an unknown machine is refused when the selector is built; re-authoring both JT-60SA artifacts matches the pinned OP1 and OP2 rows; and MAST's resolution and selection are unchanged. Write the landing fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-machine-keyed-selection.html, quoting the pin table's rows. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/, run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the committed revision the tests ran at and the command, and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/gs/test_machine_selection.py tests/gs/test_artifact_resolution.py tests/gs/test_artifact_geometry.py tests/gs/test_machine_identity.py tests/gs/test_description_artifact.py tests/spine_bench/test_machine_artifact_arm.py tests/spine_bench/test_shotset_labelling.py tests/spine_bench/test_parity.py; it exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. Record the base revision's failures in the same files, if any, so added failures can be judged by delta.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
